  <running_head>De Episcopatu / Q. V.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Bell. Altstedii</i> Supplem. in <i>Chamierium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">&amp; alios. Est autem hęc pro-</l>
    <l n="3">positio bimembris, primò dicimus</l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>ad Magistratum pertinere judicium de</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>religione &amp;c. formaliter.</i> Hoc mem-</l>
    <l n="6">brum ut eo magis cum altero mem-</l>
    <l n="7">bro intelligatur, tenendum est judi-</l>
    <l n="8">cium circa res Religionis &amp; Eccle-</l>
    <l n="9">siæ triplex esse, discretionis, defini-</l>
    <l n="10">tionis, &amp; executionis. Quantum</l>
    <l n="11">attinet ad judicium discretionis, per-</l>
    <l n="12">tinet illud ad omnes homines, adeo-</l>
    <l n="13">que etiam consequenter, imò magis</l>
    <l n="14">ad Magistratum, idq; omni tempore,</l>
    <l n="15">speciatim ante Synodum, in Synodo</l>
    <l n="16">post Synodum. Quantum ad judicií</l>
    <l n="17">definitivum (quod ita vocatur ab</l>
    <l n="18">orthodoxis per accidens, nim. respe-</l>
    <l n="19">ctu verbi Dei, cui per se unicè judi-</l>
    <l n="20">cium definitivum competit) conve-</l>
    <l n="21">nit illud Magistratui &amp; in Synodo,</l>
    <l n="22">ita ut habeat suffragium decisivum</l>
    <l n="23">æquè ac Doctores Ecclesiæ, &amp; post</l>
    <l n="24">Synodum, quando aut à parte con-</l>
    <l n="25">demnatâ, querela defertur ad Magi-</l>
    <l n="26">stratum,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The "Q." of "Quantum" carries a swash flourish; the "ii" of "judicií" is slightly doubtful (possibly a macron-type mark), read as printed. The line "stratum," is set right-aligned at the foot of the column. No marginal notes, catchword or signature are printed on this page.</notes>
</page>
